# Security & Compliance Rules

## Product tiers

- **Spectral Training** (default): rules below apply in full.
- **Spectral Operations** (`SPECTRAL_EDITION=operations`): see `.cursor/rules/11-operations-edition.mdc` and `docs/operations/SPECTRAL_OPERATIONS_CHARTER.md`. Server-side propagation permitted; tenant-isolated customer data permitted; live feeds require per-contract legal review.

## ITAR Compliance (Training tier)
Spectral Training is designed to be ITAR-compliant. This means:

1. **No classified technical data** — all platform specs, sensor parameters, and weapons data must come from publicly available sources (manufacturer datasheets, official government releases, verified open-source reporting).

2. **No export-controlled algorithms in client bundles** — Training tier does not ship ECCN 7D994/7E994-class solvers. Operations tier runs approved models server-side only per Operations charter.

3. **No real-time operational data (Training)** — do not integrate live tracking data without legal review. Operations tier uses pluggable feed adapters behind contract gate.

4. **Seed data is OSINT** — document sources in `description` fields.

## Authentication & Authorisation

- All routes except `/login` and `/register` are protected by `middleware.ts`
- `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` must NEVER appear in client-side code
- AWS Bedrock credentials (`AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID`, `AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY`) are server-only
- Mapbox and Cesium tokens are `NEXT_PUBLIC_` — acceptable (domain-restricted)

## Supabase Client Tiers — Three Tiers, Never Mix

| Client | File | Key | RLS | When to use |
|--------|------|-----|-----|-------------|
| Browser | `lib/supabase/client.ts` | anon | enforced | Client components only |
| Server | `lib/supabase/server.ts createClient()` | anon + cookies | enforced | Server components, API routes |
| Service | `lib/supabase/server.ts createServiceClient()` | service role | bypassed | Admin ops only — explicit call |
| Node | `lib/supabase/service-role-node.ts` | service role | bypassed | PCM WorldStateEngine, scripts |

**NEVER** import `createServiceClient()` from a client component or page.
**NEVER** import `service-role-node.ts` from anything under `app/` — it is for Node.js scripts and PCM only.

## Demo Mode — Production Safety

`NEXT_PUBLIC_DEMO_MODE=true` bypasses all authentication and auto-elevates the server client
to service role (bypasses RLS). This is intentional for local development ONLY.

**Critical rules:**
- `NEXT_PUBLIC_DEMO_MODE` must NEVER be set to `true` in Vercel production or staging environments
- `isDemoMode()` must NOT be true when `SPECTRAL_EDITION=operations`
- If you see `isDemoMode()` returning true in a non-local context, treat it as a P0 security incident

